    "title": "Tales from the Light Rail - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago The City of Phoenix recently completed a 5.5-mile extension of the Valley Metro light rail, connecting South Phoenix to Downtown Phoenix. The city can now brag about having a “two-line system” where the A line goes east/west and the B line goes north/south. Previously, the rail line was an L-shaped system that connected North Phoenix to Downtown Phoenix to the East Valley. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
